  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through Thursday)\nIssued at 1201 AM CDT Fri May 15 2026\n\nDry and windy conditions expected for Sunday and Monday as the\nmain H500 trough digs into the central Rockies with a series of \nperturbations moving through and just north of the Panhandles \ndownstream. Will be watching for critical fire weather conditions\nthese days as well Panhandles wide. Latest global model data \ntrends is shifting the main H850-500 moisture transport axis to \nthe east into western and central Oklahoma. Unfortunately, our \nrain chances should be shifting east as well. After hot \ntemperatures well above average for Sunday and Monday, we should \nsee a cold front move south into the Panhandles which should give \nus a break from the heat by mid week. Rain chances along and \nbehind the front may also return towards the end of the long term \nforecast period. Highs on Tuesday through Thursday will be near to\nslightly below average for mid May.",
